            "output": "---\nlayout: Conceptual\nmonikers:\n- msvc-140\n- msvc-150\n- msvc-160\n- msvc-170\n- msvc-180\ndefaultMoniker: msvc-170\nversioningType: Ranged\ntitle: /Fd (Program Database File Name) | Microsoft Learn\ncanonicalUrl: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/reference/fd-program-database-file-name?view=msvc-170\nconfig_moniker_range: '>= msvc-140'\nbreadcrumb_path: ../../_breadcrumb/toc.json\nuhfHeaderId: MSDocsHeader-CPP\nROBOTS: INDEX,FOLLOW\nmanager: coxford\nms.date: 2016-11-04T00:00:00.0000000Z\nms.topic: reference\naudience: developer\nms.service: visual-cpp\nms.tgt_pltfrm: Windows\nms.workload:\n- cplusplus\nfeedback_system: Standard\nfeedback_product_url: https://developercommunity.visualstudio.com/cpp/\nfeedback_help_link_url: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/tags/314/cpp\nfeedback_help_link_type: get-help-at-qna\nms.subservice: tools\nms.update-cycle: 1825-days\nauthor: TylerMSFT\nms.author: twhitney\ndescription: 'Learn more about: /Fd (Program Database File Name)'\nlocale: en-us\ndocument_id: d8135d7d-0a2b-8a7e-ebb5-b0e4faf3cb57\ndocument_version_independent_id: fb54a3c7-f3fa-dda4-e112-957de4770810\nupdated_at: 2025-08-23T05:03:00.0000000Z\noriginal_content_git_url: https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/cpp-docs-pr/blob/live/docs/build/reference/fd-program-database-file-name.md\ngitcommit: https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/cpp-docs-pr/blob/b3fb9c6330f286c9bb0600fa180ffd27b89c4387/docs/build/reference/fd-program-database-file-name.md\ngit_commit_id: b3fb9c6330f286c9bb0600fa180ffd27b89c4387\ndefault_moniker: msvc-170\nsite_name: Docs\ndepot_name: VS.vcppdocs\npage_type: conceptual\ntoc_rel: ../toc.json\npdf_url_template: https://learn.microsoft.com/pdfstore/en-us/VS.vcppdocs/{branchName}{pdfName}\nsearch.mshattr.devlang: cpp\nword_count: 201\nasset_id: build/reference/fd-program-database-file-name\nmoniker_range_name: 4581682a33ffa46eb75263dee4d6680e\nmonikers:\n- msvc-140\n- msvc-150\n- msvc-160\n- msvc-170\n- msvc-180\nitem_type: Content\nsource_path: docs/build/reference/fd-program-database-file-name.md\ncmProducts:\n- https://authoring-docs-microsoft.poolparty.biz/devrel/4628cbd9-6f47-4ae1-b371-d34636609eaf\nspProducts:\n- https://authoring-docs-microsoft.poolparty.biz/devrel/be21deb8-8c64-44b0-b71f-2dc56ca7364f\nplatformId: bace4fa6-2b4a-4a66-aff9-ed51e0caebab\n---\n\n# /Fd (Program Database File Name) | Microsoft Learn\n\nSpecifies a file name for the program database (PDB) file created by [/Z7, /Zi, /ZI (Debug Information Format)](z7-zi-zi-debug-information-format).\r\n\r\n## Syntax\r\n\r\n```\r\n/Fdpathname\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Remarks\r\n\r\nWithout **/Fd**, the PDB file name defaults to VC*x*0.pdb, where *x* is the major version of Visual C++ in use.\r\n\r\nIf you specify a path name that does not include a file name (the path ends in backslash), the compiler creates a .pdb file named VC*x*0.pdb in the specified directory.\r\n\r\nIf you specify a file name that does not include an extension, the compiler uses .pdb as the extension.\r\n\r\nThis option also names the state (.idb) file used for minimal rebuild and incremental compilation.\r\n\r\n### To set this compiler option in the Visual Studio development environment\r\n\r\n1. Open the project's **Property Pages** dialog box. For details, see [Set C++ compiler and build properties in Visual Studio](../working-with-project-properties).\r\n2. Select the **Configuration Properties** &gt; **C/C++** &gt; **Output Files** property page.\r\n3. Modify the **Program Database File Name** property.\r\n\r\n### To set this compiler option programmatically\r\n\r\n- See [ProgramDataBaseFileName](/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.visualstudio.vcprojectengine.vcclcompilertool.programdatabasefilename).\r\n\r\n## Example\r\n\r\nThis command line creates a .pdb file named PROG.pdb and an .idb file named PROG.idb:\r\n\r\n```cmd\r\nCL /DDEBUG /Zi /FdPROG.PDB PROG.CPP\r\n```",
